 "note": "RPCS3 Core 918 = Core 917 plus the duration of the active waits. REWINDBOX_BUSY_WAIT_REFERENCE_918: utils::busy_wait(n) is (n / 100) * scale ticks of the system counter; the build 718 journals show cntfrq=1000000000 timer_scale=1 at every boot, so busy_wait(300) lasted 3 ns against the 125 ns of the 24 MHz reference counter, 42 times less, at its 66 call sites (the wait of an SPU GETLLAR on a line a PUTLLC holds, DMA, PUTLLUC, the reservation locks, the spin of shared_mutex before its kernel wait): the waiter went on to std::this_thread::yield() or to a kernel wait almost at once. With SPU Spin Timing = Reference the scale is now the counter frequency over 24 MHz, rounded (1 on the reference counter, 42 at 1 GHz); its own setting, Automatic = every title, Disabled = the previous scale; Calibrated and the GETLLAR tick thresholds are unchanged; no wait condition changes. COREPROF SCHED918 reports the context switches, Mach traps and BSD system calls of the process per report window. Core 917 (pinned a7d1b9a6, not delivered alone): a writer that waits for the PPU threads to park spins for 8 us in a loop in front of its previous wait; park counters; the heavy PUTLLC trace and a PPU region profile asked once per boot on a storm. With the settings on Automatic the report compares the four combinations of the two levers between its windows, in three passes per boot, then leaves both on. No resolution, precision, frame limit, SPU count or priority or LLVM option changes. No codegen input changes: identities unchanged. Host bridge 8977315e unchanged; MoltenVK dependency of run 42733987255 (library d19d3a42). Built by the RPCS3 Core route (run 42776454670, attempt 1, source 02b9bf22; Apple host harnesses run 42776454670 on 02b9bf22). Verified offline on the downloaded artifacts with the repository verifier (pin_errors and bundle). Not measured on the iPhone; no FPS claim.",
